# No em dashes in UI

Never use the em dash character (`—`) in user-facing UI text (labels, headings, descriptions, buttons, toasts, empty states, marketing copy, tooltips, alt text, meta descriptions shown as UI, etc.).

## Replace with

- Persian: comma `،`, period `.`, or rephrase with `و` / a new clause
- English: comma `,`, colon `:`, parentheses, or a short rewrite
- Missing/empty numeric placeholder: use `-` or `نامشخص`, not `—`

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
"آثار تازه کاربران — پرامپت و مدل را ببینید"
"JPG، PNG، WEBP — حداکثر ۶ مگابایت"
`?? "—"`

// ✅ GOOD
"آثار تازه کاربران؛ پرامپت و مدل را ببینید"
"JPG، PNG، WEBP، حداکثر ۶ مگابایت"
`?? "-"`
```

## Out of scope

Code comments, internal docs, and model prompts may keep em dashes. This rule is for anything the user reads on the site.
